;&lt;/a&gt; &lt;img src=&quot;https://mshibanami.github.io/GitHubTrendingRSS/assets/icons/star.png&quot; width=&quot;20&quot; height=&quot;20&quot; alt=&quot;star&quot; style=&quot;margin: 0 4px 0 0; padding: 0; display: inline-block; vertical-align: middle;&quot; /&gt;2.1k &lt;img src=&quot;https://mshibanami.github.io/GitHubTrendingRSS/assets/icons/git-fork.png&quot; width=&quot;20&quot; height=&quot;20&quot; alt=&quot;git-fork&quot; style=&quot;margin: 0 4px 0 0; padding: 0; display: inline-block; vertical-align: middle;&quot; /&gt;428&lt;br&gt;Open Source Invoicing Solution for Individuals &amp;amp; Businesses&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/usepackyard/packyard&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;packyard&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt; &lt;img src=&quot;https://mshibanami.github.io/GitHubTrendingRSS/assets/icons/star.png&quot; width=&quot;20&quot; height=&quot;20&quot; alt=&quot;star&quot; style=&quot;margin: 0 4px 0 0; padding: 0; display: inline-block; vertical-align: middle;&quot; /&gt;12 &lt;img src=&quot;https://mshibanami.github.io/GitHubTrendingRSS/assets/icons/git-fork.png&quot; width=&quot;20&quot; height=&quot;20&quot; alt=&quot;git-fork&quot; style=&quot;margin: 0 4px 0 0; padding: 0; display: inline-block; vertical-align: middle;&quot; /&gt;0&lt;br&gt;Your own private Composer registry. Self-hosted, single binary, syncs PHP packages from GitHub and GitLab.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/gdarko/lexito&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;lexito&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt; &lt;img src=&quot;https://mshibanami.github.io/GitHubTrendingRSS/assets/icons/star.png&quot; width=&quot;20&quot; height=&quot;20&quot; alt=&quot;star&quot; style=&quot;margin: 0 4px 0 0; padding: 0; display: inline-block; vertical-align: middle;&quot; /&gt;3 &lt;img src=&quot;https://mshibanami.github.io/GitHubTrendingRSS/assets/icons/git-fork.png&quot; width=&quot;20&quot; height=&quot;20&quot; alt=&quot;git-fork&quot; style=&quot;margin: 0 4px 0 0; padding: 0; display: inline-block; vertical-align: middle;&quot; /&gt;0&lt;br&gt;AI-assisted gettext (.po/.mo) translation editor for macOS and Linux written in Rust and Iced&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/gdarko/cyberdeck&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;cyberdeck&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt; &lt;img src=&quot;https://mshibanami.github.io/GitHubTrendingRSS/assets/icons/star.png&quot; width=&quot;20&quot; height=&quot;20&quot; alt=&quot;star&quot; style=&quot;margin: 0 4px 0 0; padding: 0; display: inline-block; vertical-align: middle;&quot; /&gt;0 &lt;img src=&quot;https://mshibanami.github.io/GitHubTrendingRSS/assets/icons/git-fork.png&quot; width=&quot;20&quot; height=&quot;20&quot; alt=&quot;git-fork&quot; style=&quot;margin: 0 4px 0 0; padding: 0; display: inline-block; vertical-align: middle;&quot; /&gt;0&lt;br&gt;Tiny WiFi-connected ESP8266 gadget with a 16x2 LCD that lives on my desk, cycling between live weather, currency rates, and system health on button press.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/gdarko/eter&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;eter&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt; &lt;img src=&quot;https://mshibanami.github.io/GitHubTrendingRSS/assets/icons/star.png&quot; width=&quot;20&quot; height=&quot;20&quot; alt=&quot;star&quot; style=&quot;margin: 0 4px 0 0; padding: 0; display: inline-block; vertical-align: middle;&quot; /&gt;0 &lt;img src=&quot;https://mshibanami.github.io/GitHubTrendingRSS/assets/icons/git-fork.png&quot; width=&quot;20&quot; height=&quot;20&quot; alt=&quot;git-fork&quot; style=&quot;margin: 0 4px 0 0; padding: 0; display: inline-block; vertical-align: middle;&quot; /&gt;0&lt;br&gt;Personal radio player that lives in my menubar on Mac and Linux. It works on Windows too.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;hr&gt;&lt;h1&gt;Hi, I&#39;m Darko.&lt;/h1&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;I am a &lt;strong&gt;software architect and senior engineer building trustworthy AI systems&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;For 12+ years I have worked across product engineering, system architecture, cloud infrastructure, reliability, performance, and security. I like owning the whole path from an ambiguous product problem to a system a team can operate safely.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;Right now I am applying that experience to agentic software: explicit identity, narrow tool contracts, retrieval and context, repeatable evaluation, human control, and safe failure modes. I am interested in useful automation, not impressive demos without a production contract.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;I am open to remote &lt;strong&gt;Software Architect&lt;/strong&gt;, &lt;strong&gt;Senior/Staff Software Engineer&lt;/strong&gt;, and &lt;strong&gt;AI Systems Engineer&lt;/strong&gt; roles with international product and platform teams.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;h2&gt;What I work on&lt;/h2&gt; 
&lt;ul&gt; 
 &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;AI systems engineering&lt;/strong&gt; — agent workflows, tools, evaluation, context, memory, and human approval&lt;/li&gt; 
 &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Software architecture&lt;/strong&gt; — boundaries, interfaces, quality attributes, trade-offs, and system evolution&lt;/li&gt; 
 &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Production engineering&lt;/strong&gt; — delivery, Kubernetes, observability, reliability, performance, and cost&lt;/li&gt; 
 &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Security by design&lt;/strong&gt; — identity, least privilege, threat modeling, data protection, and supply-chain risk&lt;/li&gt; 
&lt;/ul&gt; 
&lt;h2&gt;Selected shipped systems&lt;/h2&gt; 
&lt;ul&gt; 
 &lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/InvoiceShelf/InvoiceShelf&quot;&gt;InvoiceShelf&lt;/a&gt; — core maintainer; multi-tenancy, cross-layer refactoring, typed front-end migration, and AI-assisted invoice scanning work&lt;/li&gt; 
 &lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://darkog.com/projects/celersearch&quot;&gt;CelerSearch&lt;/a&gt; — managed search platform; Go control plane, customer portal, billing, and WordPress integration; 2,000+ Meilisearch instances deployed&lt;/li&gt; 
 &lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://darkog.com/projects/megaoptim&quot;&gt;MegaOptim&lt;/a&gt; — image optimization product serving 1,000+ websites and applications&lt;/li&gt; 
 &lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://packyard.dev/&quot;&gt;Packyard&lt;/a&gt; — self-hosted Composer registry distributed as a single Go binary&lt;/li&gt; 
 &lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/gdarko/lexito&quot;&gt;Lexito&lt;/a&gt; — AI-assisted Gettext translation editor for macOS and Linux&lt;/li&gt; 
&lt;/ul&gt; 
&lt;h2&gt;Current reference work&lt;/h2&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;I am building two public AI-systems labs. Both use synthetic scenarios and publish repeatable evaluation artifacts. They are &lt;strong&gt;reference implementations, not client production deployments&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;ul&gt; 
 &lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/gdarko/tenant-safe-support-agent&quot;&gt;Tenant-safe Support Agent&lt;/a&gt; — LangGraph workflow with tool-side tenant enforcement, cited evidence, approval-gated writes, a threat model, and a committed 120-case deterministic policy baseline&lt;/li&gt; 
 &lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/gdarko/guarded-incident-response-agent&quot;&gt;Guarded Incident-response Agent&lt;/a&gt; — Kubernetes diagnosis workflow with a credential-free agent, narrow broker RBAC, exact approvals, a committed 60-case baseline, and an isolated live-lab check&lt;/li&gt; 
&lt;/ul&gt; 
&lt;h2&gt;Elsewhere&lt;/h2&gt; 
&lt;ul&gt; 
 &lt;li&gt;Portfolio and case studies: &lt;a href=&quot;https://darkog.com&quot;&gt;darkog.com&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt; 
 &lt;li&gt;CV: &lt;a href=&quot;https://darkog.com/darko-gjorgjijoski-cv.pdf&quot;&gt;darkog.com/darko-gjorgjijoski-cv.pdf&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt; 
 &lt;li&gt;LinkedIn: &lt;a href=&quot;https://linkedin.com/in/gdarko&quot;&gt;linkedin.com/in/gdarko&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt; 
 &lt;li&gt;Contact: &lt;a href=&quot;mailto:hi@darkog.com&quot;&gt;hi@darkog.com&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt; 
&lt;/ul&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;I write direct, practical notes about AI systems, architecture, production engineering, and security—usually after testing the idea against real constraints.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
      
